1
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:14,360
(11:50-12:00 PM)

2
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:19,400
(11:50-12:00 PM)

3
00:00:20,434 --> 00:00:23,746
♪Your silhouette melts into the glow♪

4
00:00:25,207 --> 00:00:26,515
(Congrats to our grand prize winner!
Prize money: 100,000 yuan)

5
00:00:27,122 --> 00:00:30,642
♪I count your sighs♪

6
00:00:32,216 --> 00:00:34,584
♪Every breath♪

7
00:00:34,584 --> 00:00:37,336
♪Feels like I'm stealing♪

8
00:00:39,365 --> 00:00:40,645
♪The next second♪

9
00:00:41,349 --> 00:00:44,101
♪Before it's no longer mine♪

10
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:49,900
♪We live♪
(Capernaum)

11
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:54,258
♪In the spaces between moments♪

12
00:00:55,767 --> 00:01:01,079
♪Breathing through each other's shadows♪

13
00:01:01,889 --> 00:01:04,449
♪Let's not speak of what's to come♪

14
00:01:04,926 --> 00:01:07,998
♪Or what came before♪

15
00:01:09,459 --> 00:01:14,835
♪This moment could last me a lifetime♪
(12:00-11:50 PM)

16
00:01:17,459 --> 00:01:20,723
=Thirteen Types of Love=
=Episode 12=

17
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:23,340
Let me be your assistant.

18
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:25,220
I won't let anyone push you around.

19
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:26,620
I'll protect you.

20
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:31,140
We just met.

21
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:32,420
And you're already trying to protect me?

22
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:36,820
Isn't that a little weird?

23
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:40,020
Fair point.

24
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:45,260
Let's do another take.

25
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:48,460
I'm from 100 years in the future...

26
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:49,100
Miss Lin!

27
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:49,940
Miss Lin, hurry!

28
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:51,300
Our male lead said yes!

29
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:51,980
We've got to hurry.

30
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:52,940
Talk later, hero!

31
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:54,380
I'll shoot scene 1-5 first.

32
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:56,100
Give me another chance. I'm...

33
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:57,380
Wardrobe!

34
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:58,740
She's here. Get her changed.

35
00:01:59,220 --> 00:01:59,780
Okay!

36
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:00,780
Didn't we just finish that scene?

37
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:01,500
Duo, you got this!

38
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:02,940
The lead doesn't have much time.

39
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:04,100
We can only shoot one more scene.

40
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,620
The director wants the key scene.

41
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:07,340
Quick, go over your lines.

42
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:08,380
The lead's got a temper.

43
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:09,580
Don't mess up again.

44
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:16,820
Come on, gorgeous! Hurry!

45
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:18,700
Get up here!

46
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:20,380
Just lie down right there.

47
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:21,420
Terminal cancer.

48
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:23,020
Listen,

49
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:25,180
you've just talked to Dr. Gao

50
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:26,500
about the cost of further treatment.

51
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:27,820
You're outside,
trying to pull yourself together.

52
00:02:28,340 --> 00:02:29,260
How's Duo doing?

53
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,820
The cancer's spreading fast.

54
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:32,060
Prepare for the worst.

55
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:34,340
We'll shoot that scene later.

56
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:35,900
Anyway, three, two, one.

57
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,140
You come in from here

58
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:39,940
and put down the buns and helmet.

59
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:41,900
Then take off

60
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:42,980
the raincoat right here.

61
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,100
Then go get cozy
with that gorgeous girl.

62
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:46,220
At this point,

63
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:47,540
I still don't know

64
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:48,780
I came from 100 years in the future

65
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,300
to save my wife.

66
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:50,940
Exactly.

67
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:51,860
That comes later.

68
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:52,940
This is the beginning.

69
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,220
Before the time travel.

70
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:55,900
Got it.

71
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:56,660
Understood.

72
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:57,580
Good.

73
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:58,420
Let's try a take, okay?

74
00:02:58,620 --> 00:02:58,980
Sure!

75
00:03:01,176 --> 00:03:04,860
♪Through one world after another♪

76
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:05,540
Sure. No problem.

77
00:03:08,177 --> 00:03:11,380
♪You're still my only way home♪

78
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:12,420
(That can't be real!)

79
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:13,460
(Is this fake?)

80
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:15,060
(YAA 80968)

81
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:16,180
(This is so unreal!)

82
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:17,780
(It's just like a movie!)

83
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,956
♪You're where my time ends♪

84
00:03:19,956 --> 00:03:21,492
♪My way forward♪

85
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:23,340
(This feels so strange.)

86
00:03:23,340 --> 00:03:24,740
♪Gives way to you♪

87
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:25,660
(I can't tell what's real anymore.)

88
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,940
♪As the monsoon shifts around the bend♪

89
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:28,620
(Yongsen,)

90
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:30,460
♪I'm still where we first met♪

91
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,580
(I don't want this.)

92
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:36,060
(If only none of this were real.)

93
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:40,210
♪You're still my one and only song♪

94
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:44,434
♪Though the world breaks into dust♪

95
00:03:44,434 --> 00:03:45,949
♪At the end of time♪

96
00:03:46,499 --> 00:03:48,624
♪I wait for your echo♪

97
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:12,180
Duo.

98
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:14,340
Do you remember me?

99
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:16,700
The system told me

100
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:19,740
you're the one I love most.

101
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:28,260
Memorize the process
of debugging the system's internal data.

102
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:30,580
Make it second nature.

103
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:32,300
Just take it in.

104
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:35,300
Feel it with your heart.

105
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:44,460
(Warning.)

106
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:48,220
(Subject Zhang Yongsen is
under extreme emotional stress.)

107
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,940
(His consciousness is deeply confused.)

108
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:53,380
(The current universe will absorb him.)

109
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:54,700
(He will disappear completely.)

110
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:56,420
(Warning.)

111
00:04:56,780 --> 00:05:00,380
(Subject Zhang Yongsen is
under extreme emotional stress.)

112
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:01,580
Don't be afraid.

113
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:03,260
(His consciousness is deeply confused.)

114
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:05,860
(The current universe will absorb him.)

115
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:07,140
(He will disappear completely.)

116
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:09,100
(Warning.)

117
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:13,260
(Subject Zhang Yongsen is
under extreme emotional stress.)

118
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:16,380
(His consciousness is deeply confused.)

119
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:18,940
(The current universe will absorb him.)

120
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,220
(He will disappear completely.)

121
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,380
(Due to earlier forced intervention,)

122
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,500
(Subject Zhang Yongsen's consciousness)

123
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:28,420
(has caused multiple breaches
in Universe 3C-091NB.)

124
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,940
(Chamber 6 Operating Normally)
(Multiple universes are leaking in.)

125
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:32,740
(Subject Zhang Yongsen sees
overlapping realities.)

126
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:33,740
(His consciousness is collapsing.)

127
00:05:33,860 --> 00:05:35,740
(He will disappear in five minutes.)

128
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:37,260
Try jumping.

129
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:38,700
Bring the subject's mind back.

130
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:40,300
(Subject Zhang Yongsen)

131
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:42,580
(is unconscious.)

132
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,060
(Consciousness jump unavailable.)

133
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,540
(Subject Zhang Yongsen)

134
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:47,860
(is unconscious.)

135
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,300
(Consciousness jump unavailable.)

136
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,220
Quiet!

137
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:56,380
Subject 108 is a success so far.

138
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:59,020
Self-awareness takes time

139
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:00,740
to adjust and fully develop.

140
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,460
But still,

141
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:03,700
it's only a matter of time.

142
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:08,100
If that's true,

143
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:11,540
you really don't need to come back.

144
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:15,980
But if Subject 108 fails this time,

145
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:17,340
in the near future,

146
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:19,700
I won't be able

147
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:22,100
to find a better-matched

148
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:25,740
subject consciousness
in another universe.

149
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:30,380
And even if I went in to save you,

150
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:33,620
I couldn't pull it off.

151
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:36,500
(Subject Zhang Yongsen's
consciousness is fading.)

152
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:38,260
(Final countdown begins.)

153
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,020
(Five.)

154
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:41,660
(Four.)

155
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,060
(Three.)

156
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:44,340
(Two.)

157
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:46,380
(One.)

158
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:48,060
Who is it?

159
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,700
(I'm Lin Duo.)

160
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:55,980
(The moment you open your eyes,)

161
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:57,860
(you'll believe)

162
00:06:59,020 --> 00:06:59,740
(I)

163
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:02,260
(am Lin Duo.)

164
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:22,740
The doctor said to get more rest.

165
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:24,580
You should be fine.

166
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:27,140
These things

167
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:28,580
were left after your examination.

168
00:07:29,180 --> 00:07:30,100
See if anything's missing.

169
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:33,380
Thanks.

170
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:51,980
Have you seen a little bottle

171
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:53,340
with red liquid inside?

172
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:55,580
Everything you had is here.

173
00:07:58,260 --> 00:07:58,660
Oh no.

174
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:01,460
If it's gone, I'm done for.

175
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:04,180
Is it important?

176
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:10,620
What's wrong?

177
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,100
Here, sit down.

178
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:12,820
Sit.

179
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:22,220
That's a bit rude.

180
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:24,220
Sorry.

181
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:26,820
It smells sweet.

182
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:29,260
It's not perfume.

183
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:33,780
I dreamed about you last night.

184
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:37,620
I've never had such a vivid dream.

185
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:41,300
I wanted to talk to you about it,

186
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:43,420
but with everything going on,

187
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:44,340
now isn't a good time.

188
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:45,860
So,

189
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:47,660
let's do this another time.

190
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:21,100
Hey.

191
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:32,140
Let's leave.

192
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:48,580
Duo.

193
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:51,740
You've already ordered coffee?

194
00:09:54,340 --> 00:09:55,100
That perfume...

195
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,180
It smells so sweet.

196
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:58,380
But it's different from last time.

197
00:09:58,780 --> 00:09:59,380
Do you like it?

198
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:01,260
I asked you here today

199
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:03,060
to talk about that dream.

200
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:04,580
I dreamed

201
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:07,780
that I died in front of you many times.

202
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:08,700
What?

203
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:10,660
The first time was just like the script.

204
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:12,460
The one from the other day,

205
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:13,580
the crew we ran into.

206
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:16,500
Then I caught an infectious disease.

207
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:18,220
And then

208
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:19,980
after you died,

209
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:21,180
I took my own life.

210
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:22,500
There was another time,

211
00:10:22,740 --> 00:10:23,580
but it's really hazy.

212
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:24,740
When I woke up,

213
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:26,140
I couldn't remember it.

214
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:26,900
Impossible.

215
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,020
You couldn't possibly know any of this.

216
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:30,980
I'm from 100 years in the future.

217
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:32,140
And you belong to a separate universe.

218
00:10:32,220 --> 00:10:33,020
How could you possibly know?

219
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:38,700
Where was I?

220
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:42,260
You said you came back from 100 years
in the future to save me.

221
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:48,820
No reset?

222
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:50,260
Why?

223
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:52,340
You're asking me?

224
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:54,580
Something's wrong.

225
00:10:57,580 --> 00:10:59,500
I came back from 100 years in the future
to save my wife.

226
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,260
What you just said

227
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:02,140
sounds exactly like

228
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:03,860
the lines from scene 1-1.

229
00:11:04,180 --> 00:11:05,060
The original line was

230
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:08,540
"I time-jumped here
from 100 years in the future."

231
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:11,820
- "I'm here to save my wife."
- "I'm here to save my wife."

232
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:17,140
That line is a time code.

233
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:19,220
But in this universe,

234
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,180
it's already been defined.

235
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:21,900
So the glitch can't be used,

236
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:23,020
and I can't jump.

237
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:24,820
Wait.

238
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:27,260
That wasn't in the original script.

239
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:29,100
Say it again. I'll write it down.

240
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:37,540
Duo.

241
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:42,900
If I couldn't reload endlessly,

242
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:43,380
then...

243
00:11:44,060 --> 00:11:45,300
how could I ever protect you?

244
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,620
Do I need protecting?

245
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:00,700
Well, I do.

246
00:12:07,414 --> 00:12:11,056
(Rebooting)

247
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:19,740
Let me be honest with you.

248
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:24,220
No, don't say it.

249
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,540
You don't have it in you.

250
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:29,740
Actually, I do have something to say.

251
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:31,420
Just one thing.

252
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:33,060
Well...

253
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:36,180
Go on, then.

254
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:39,100
Duo,

255
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:42,100
we've been together for so long.

256
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:45,380
But this time feels strange.

257
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,540
I have this...

258
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,060
feeling.

259
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:49,820
Like

260
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:52,060
we've gone back

261
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:53,900
to right after graduation.

262
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:56,300
Yongsen...

263
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:00,180
Marry me.

264
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:04,820
We don't have to wait for sunrise.

265
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:07,460
Or for the rain to stop.

266
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:15,100
I do.

267
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:16,820
♪Love leaves us empty, I won't deny it♪

268
00:13:16,820 --> 00:13:17,740
Let's get married tomorrow.

269
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:18,970
♪But back then♪

270
00:13:18,970 --> 00:13:20,020
♪I never thought it'd end this way♪

271
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:21,500
As soon as the sun rises.

272
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:24,380
As soon as the rain stops.

273
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:28,540
Duo.

274
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:30,500
♪I've tried so hard to live alone♪

275
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:31,340
It really is you.

276
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:33,580
♪And learned not to ask what if♪

277
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:34,420
You're back.

278
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:39,580
No.

279
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:43,002
♪Time is empty, I no longer count♪

280
00:13:43,538 --> 00:13:44,528
♪Those tender moments♪

281
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:46,620
You never left.

282
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:51,920
♪Taught me what it all meant♪

283
00:13:53,403 --> 00:13:56,091
♪I face the emptiness in peace♪

284
00:13:56,596 --> 00:14:00,455
♪Though sometimes I still envy♪

285
00:14:06,343 --> 00:14:09,632
♪Only after loss are we complete♪

286
00:14:11,345 --> 00:14:16,081
♪Loss is a lesson we must learn♪

287
